---
title: Scenario 3 — Trace a value through an unfamiliar codebase (confirm mode, one action denied)
---
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor U as User
    participant CLI as CLI Interface
    participant L as Agentic Loop
    participant LLM as LLM (Ollama / Groq)
    participant T as Tools / MCP Client
    participant FS as Filesystem MCP Server
    participant SH as Local Tools (search_code / run_shell)

    U->>CLI: "Raise the HTTP timeout to 30s and check nothing else uses the old value"
    CLI->>L: submit task (confirm mode)

    Note over L,LLM: 1. Orient in the codebase
    L->>LLM: history + tool schemas
    LLM-->>L: tool_call list_directory(".")
    L->>CLI: show tool call (read-only, no prompt)
    L->>T: list_directory(".")
    T->>FS: MCP call list_directory
    FS-->>T: entries
    T-->>L: result

    Note over L,SH: 2. Find every use of the value
    L->>LLM: history + listing
    LLM-->>L: tool_call search_code("timeout")
    L->>CLI: show tool call (read-only, no prompt)
    L->>T: search_code("timeout")
    T->>SH: regex scan of the working tree
    SH-->>T: 3 matches (config.py, client.py, tests/)
    T-->>L: result
    L->>LLM: history + matches
    LLM-->>L: tool_call read_text_file("config.py")
    L->>T: read_text_file("config.py")
    T->>FS: MCP call read_text_file
    FS-->>T: file contents
    T-->>L: result

    Note over CLI,U: 3. Edit, with confirmation
    L->>LLM: history + file contents
    LLM-->>L: tool_call edit_file(config.py, TIMEOUT 10 -> 30)
    L->>CLI: show tool call + diff
    CLI->>U: "Allow edit_file? [y/n/a]"
    U-->>CLI: y
    CLI-->>L: approved
    L->>T: edit_file(...)
    T->>FS: MCP call edit_file
    FS-->>T: success
    T-->>L: result

    Note over CLI,U: 4. A denied action, and recovery
    L->>LLM: history + edit result
    LLM-->>L: tool_call run_shell("pip install -U httpx")
    L->>CLI: show tool call
    CLI->>U: "Allow run_shell: pip install -U httpx? [y/n/a]"
    U-->>CLI: n
    CLI-->>L: denied
    L->>LLM: history + "user denied run_shell"
    Note right of LLM: the loop continues — a denial<br/>is an observation, not a failure
    LLM-->>L: tool_call search_code("TIMEOUT")
    L->>T: search_code("TIMEOUT")
    T->>SH: regex scan
    SH-->>T: 1 remaining match (tests/)
    T-->>L: result

    L->>LLM: history + remaining matches
    LLM-->>L: final answer (streamed)
    L->>CLI: stream tokens
    CLI->>U: "config.py now uses 30s. tests/test_client.py still asserts 10s. Skipped the install you declined."
